WOW-BG3 vmangos patch 0025: a loot BG3 took is booked in WoW, its reach judged where BG3 took it.

BG3's loot window is where the player takes a WoW corpse's item, in reach. `loot take` reached WoW a moment
later (the inventory bridge's round trip, one call per item of a Take All), and WoW's loot handlers measure
the reach from where the body is then: a player who walked on at once was refused `far` for the last items,
and WoW's own loot window on that corpse still offered them (a playtest report). Now:

- `loot take CHAR NPC ENTRY[,ENTRY...]` takes several entries in one call (the bridge's batch of BG3's takes
  from one corpse); ENTRY is IDX, money or all, with `@X/Y/Z` when BG3 sends the looter's place at its take.
- While an entry with a place is booked, WowBg3::InLootReach measures WoW's loot reach
  (GetMaxLootDistance, as before) from that place, in WoW's own loot handlers (opening the loot, items,
  money). Everywhere else, a WoW client's own loot included, it is the looter's place now, as before.
- One reply line per entry: `take IDX ok GUID MONEY`, `take money ok|refused nothing DELTA`,
  `take ENTRY refused far|notyours|gone|full`. `loot list` is unchanged.

